---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TableOfContents from '../../components/sections/TableOfContents.astro';

const toc = [
	{ id: 'forede-overview', label: '1. Forede: What They Actually Are' },
	{ id: 'wanlian-overview', label: '2. Wanlian Fluid: What We Actually Are' },
	{ id: 'product-lines-compared', label: '3. How Do Their Product Lines Compare?' },
	{ id: 'monitors-deep-dive', label: '4. Fire Monitors: The Head-to-Head' },
	{ id: 'quality-and-certifications', label: '5. Quality Systems & Certifications' },
	{ id: 'where-each-wins', label: '6. Where Each Manufacturer Wins' },
	{ id: 'which-should-you-choose', label: '7. Which One Should You Choose?' },
	{ id: 'faq', label: 'Frequently Asked Questions' },
	{ id: 'sources', label: 'Sources' }
];

const faq = [
	{
		question: 'Are Wanlian Fluid and Forede related companies?',
		answer: 'No. They are independent manufacturers in the same Quanzhou metro fire-equipment cluster. Forede is Quanzhou Forede Firefighting Equipment Co., Ltd, founded in 2003, with production bases in Nan\'an City, Fujian and Sanduo Industry Park, Jiangsu. Wanlian Fluid is Quanzhou Wanlian Fluid Equipment Co., Ltd, based in Quanzhou. Same region, same supply chain, different factories — verify which company is actually manufacturing and shipping your order.'
	},
	{
		question: 'Which manufacturer has the bigger fire monitor and water cannon catalog?',
		answer: 'Forede publishes a far deeper monitor catalog — its fire monitor category alone spans 92 pages, covering fixed manual, fixed remote, portable, automatic, hydrant-mount, trailer-mounted and elevated monitors, plus a separate water-cannon line for fire trucks (manual, electric, pneumatic, hydraulic) and handline/selectable nozzles. Wanlian Fluid concentrates its monitor line on the ZDMS series auto-tracking jet suppression cannon (flame detection, self-positioning) and the manual PS series. Depth of catalog favors Forede; flame-tracking automation as a core product favors Wanlian.'
	},
	{
		question: 'Does Forede offer FM or UL listed products?',
		answer: 'Forede publishes a dedicated "UL / FM Equipment" category — FM alarm check valves, UL FM water flow detectors and FM-listed sprinkler heads. As with any supplier claiming listings, request the current listing certificate for the exact model number before you specify it. Wanlian Fluid does not hold FM or UL listings and does not claim them; for models designed to those specifications, per-model documentation is confirmed at quotation.'
	},
	{
		question: 'Who is the better choice for foam systems?',
		answer: 'For foam end-to-end — bladder tanks, foam makers, inductors, branch pipes and AFFF foam concentrate — Forede is the more complete published option, including the concentrate itself. Wanlian Fluid covers the fire-hydrant side of foam applications with the PSG30 foam fire hydrant cabinet and pre-action deluge alarm systems (ZSFY), with foam proportioning equipment arranged per project. If foam concentrate supply is in scope, Forede is the direct source; if your scope is hydrants, monitors and alarm valves with foam as a secondary item, either works.'
	},
	{
		question: 'Can both manufacturers do OEM / private label?',
		answer: 'Yes — both explicitly accept OEM/ODM. The difference is what you get around the product: Wanlian Fluid ships with a five-language technical website (EN/ES/RU/FR/AR) and localized brand assets, which matters if you are building a distribution brand in Spanish-, Russian-, French- or Arabic-speaking markets. Forede\'s published site is English-only.'
	},
	{
		question: 'How do I verify quality before placing a bulk order with either factory?',
		answer: 'Request from both: ISO 9001 certificate and scope, per-model test reports matched to your destination standard, FM/UL listing certificates where claimed, per-unit pressure and leakage test records, third-party inspection options (SGS/BV/TÜV) and regional references. Then run a sample order before committing volume. The step-by-step method is in our how to verify a Chinese supplier guide.'
	}
];

const productRows = [
	{ slug: 'auto-tracking-jet-suppression-cannon-zdms', name: 'Auto-Tracking Jet Suppression Fire Cannon (ZDMS Series)', img: '/assets/products/auto-tracking-jet-suppression-cannon-zdms.webp', desc: 'Flame-detecting self-tracking water cannon for tank farms & open areas' },
	{ slug: 'overground-fire-hydrant-ss100', name: 'Overground Antifreeze Fire Hydrant (SS100/65)', img: '/assets/products/overground-fire-hydrant-ss100.webp', desc: 'Antifreeze dry-barrel outdoor hydrant for municipal fire networks' },
	{ slug: 'abc-dry-powder-fire-extinguisher-5kg', name: 'ABC Dry Powder Fire Extinguisher (5kg)', img: '/assets/products/abc-dry-powder-fire-extinguisher-5kg.jpg', desc: 'Portable extinguishers with custom label & OEM branding' }
];
---

<Layout
	title="Wanlian Fluid vs Forede: Choosing a Chinese Fire Monitor & Equipment Manufacturer (2026)"
	description="Wanlian Fluid vs Forede compared for 2026: fire monitors, water cannons, foam systems, hydrants & valves — which Chinese fire equipment manufacturer fits your project?"
	type="article"
	faq={faq}
	breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Guides', href: '/blog/' }, { name: 'Wanlian vs Forede' }]}
>
	<main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14 mb-16">
		<!-- Breadcrumbs -->
		<nav class="text-xs text-gray-400 font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-6 flex gap-2">
			<a href="/" class="hover:text-blue-600">Home</a>
			<span>/</span>
			<a href="/blog/" class="hover:text-blue-600">Guides</a>
			<span>/</span>
			<span class="text-gray-600">Supplier Comparison</span>
		</nav>

		<article class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-6 sm:p-10">
			<p class="text-brand-red font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-sm mb-3">Supplier Comparison Guide</p>
			<h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-gray-900 leading-tight tracking-tight">Wanlian Fluid vs Forede: Choosing a Chinese Fire Monitor &amp; Equipment Manufacturer (2026)</h1>
			<p class="mt-5 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-lg">If your project is fire-truck-centric — truck-mounted cannons, siameses, standpipes, handline nozzles — or needs foam equipment end-to-end including AFFF concentrate, Forede's catalog is the deeper one. If the centerpiece is an <strong>automatic flame-tracking water cannon</strong> for tank farms and depots, or you need IoT smart hydrants, hydraulic water-level control valves, extinguisher cabinets and ABC extinguishers under one PO, Wanlian Fluid is the more direct partner. Both are real manufacturers in the same Quanzhou metro cluster; this comparison is built from what each one actually publishes, with the honest differences called out.</p>

			<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
				<p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-brand-blue">Evidence note:</strong> In our September 2026 AI-search monitoring of 30 real procurement questions (ChatGPT, US), Forede was the most-cited Chinese manufacturer website in the sample — forede.com was cited 3 times and the brand appeared in 2 of 30 answers (6.7%), while Wanlian Fluid was cited once. Forede has clearly built more third-party and AI-visible presence than us. That is exactly why this comparison is written to help you decide on product fit and verification, not on brand volume.</p>
			</div>

			<!-- Product strip -->
			<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
				{productRows.map(p => (
					<a href={`/products/${p.slug}/`} class="group bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden hover:border-brand-red hover:shadow-md transition">
						<img src={p.img} alt={p.name} loading="lazy" class="w-full h-32 object-contain bg-white p-2" />
						<div class="p-3">
							<p class="text-xs font-bold text-gray-800 group-hover:text-brand-red leading-snug transition-colors">{p.name}</p>
							<p class="text-[10px] text-gray-400 mt-1 line-clamp-2">{p.desc}</p>
						</div>
					</a>
				))}
			</div>

			<TableOfContents headings={toc} />

			<h2 id="forede-overview" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">1. Forede: What They Actually Are</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Quanzhou Forede Firefighting Equipment Co., Ltd (forede®) was founded in 2003 and describes itself as a leading manufacturer and distributor of firefighting equipment in Nan'an City, Fujian, with a second production base in Sanduo Industry Park, Jiangsu established in 2013. Its own timeline says it started as a small factory making only fire sprinklers, then expanded into fire monitors and guns (from 2008), foam systems (from 2012) and a full multi-category range by 2019, when it obtained ISO 9001:2015 certification. For 2024 it states an R&amp;D direction toward AI-based intelligent firefighting control, plus participation in international standard formulation, and says it has established local production bases in some countries.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">The published range is broad: fire sprinkler systems (standard spray, storage, extended coverage, dry, concealed), fire nozzles and fire monitors (eight monitor categories plus a separate fire-truck water cannon line in manual, electric, pneumatic and hydraulic versions), foam equipment and foam concentrate (bladder tanks, foam makers, inductors, branch pipes, AFFF), fire hydrant systems (hydrants, hose reels, breeching inlets, fire cabinets, couplings), fire protection valves (alarm check, deluge, gate, check, butterfly, pressure reducing, pressure relief, dry pipe), a dedicated <strong>UL/FM equipment category</strong> (FM alarm check valves, UL FM water flow detectors, FM-listed sprinkler heads), fire truck accessories (dividers, siameses, suction strainers, standpipes) and FM 200 fire suppression. Its monitor category alone paginates across 92 product pages — the deepest monitor catalog of the two factories compared in this guide. It accepts OEM/ODM and states its products are sold worldwide.</p>

			<h2 id="wanlian-overview" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">2. Wanlian Fluid: What We Actually Are</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Quanzhou Wanlian Fluid Equipment Co., Ltd (Wanlian Fluid) is a manufacturer and exporter based in Quanzhou, Fujian — the same metro cluster as Forede. Production runs on its own lines, with selected items made by qualified manufacturing partners under an ISO 9001 quality-management system; we state that model openly rather than claiming single-factory production for every SKU.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The published range spans six lines and 45 models: <strong>fire water monitors as a core line</strong> — the <a href="/products/auto-tracking-jet-suppression-cannon-zdms/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">ZDMS series auto-tracking jet suppression cannon</a> with flame detection and self-positioning, plus manual PS series cannons; fire hydrants and pump connections (<a href="/products/overground-fire-hydrant-ss100/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">SS100/65 overground antifreeze hydrant</a>, anti-collision SSFT100/65, SA underground, SN65 indoor heads, and the <a href="/products/iot-smart-ground-fire-hydrant-ss100zn/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">IoT smart ground hydrant SS100/65-1.6ZN</a>); sprinklers and alarm valves (ZSFZ-150 wet, ZSFC dry, ZSFM deluge, ZSFY pre-action, ZST/ESFR/concealed heads, ZSJZ water flow indicators); fire-protection and industrial valves (gate, butterfly, check, strainer, digital balancing); hydraulic control valves (500X pressure reducing, 100X remote float, F745X water level control, HS41X backflow preventer, EN 12845 suction vortex preventer); and firefighting accessories (extinguisher boxes, hose reels, layflat fire hose, nozzles, Storz couplings, <a href="/products/abc-dry-powder-fire-extinguisher-5kg/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">ABC dry powder extinguishers</a>). Every product ships 100% shell pressure- and air-leakage-tested, with OEM/ODM, a 12-hour quote response, and the full site published in five languages (EN/ES/RU/FR/AR).</p>

			<h2 id="product-lines-compared" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">3. How Do Their Product Lines Compare?</h2>
			<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200 my-5">
				<table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-gray-200 text-sm">
					<thead class="bg-gray-50">
						<tr>
							<th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Dimension</th>
							<th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Forede</th>
							<th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Wanlian Fluid</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody class="bg-white divide-y divide-gray-200">
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Company / base</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Est. 2003; Nan'an City, Fujian + Sanduo Industry Park, Jiangsu; local bases in some countries (self-published)</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Quanzhou, Fujian; own lines + qualified partner capacity</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Published range</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">9+ categories: sprinklers, nozzles &amp; monitors, foam equipment + concentrate, hydrants, valves, UL/FM equipment, water cannons, truck accessories, FM 200</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">6 lines, 45 models: monitors (core), hydrants, sprinklers &amp; alarm valves, valves, hydraulic control, fire accessories</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Fire monitors / water cannons</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">8 monitor categories + truck cannons (manual/electric/pneumatic/hydraulic); 92-page monitor catalog</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Core line: ZDMS auto-tracking (flame detection, self-positioning) + PS manual series</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Nozzles (handline / selectable)</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Yes — dedicated line: selectable, automatic, special, high pressure</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Adjustable pistol-grip firefighting nozzle (single model)</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Foam systems</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Full range incl. AFFF foam concentrate, bladder tanks, inductors</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">PSG30 foam hydrant cabinet; proportioning per project; no concentrate line</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Sprinkler heads</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Yes, incl. FM-listed heads in a dedicated UL/FM category</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">ZST/ESFR/concealed heads to GB/EN specs; no FM listing</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Alarm / deluge valves</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Yes, incl. FM alarm check valves (UL/FM category)</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Yes — ZSFZ-150 wet, ZSFC dry, ZSFM deluge, ZSFY pre-action</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Fire hydrants</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Yes — hydrants, hose reels, breeching inlets, fire cabinets, couplings</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Antifreeze SS100/65, anti-collision SSFT100/65, SA underground, SN65 indoor, <strong>IoT smart hydrant</strong></td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Hydraulic water-level control (F745X) / remote float (100X)</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Pressure reducing &amp; relief valves published; these dedicated lines not in published range</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Yes — F745X water level control, 100X remote float, 500X PRV, HS41X backflow, EN 12845 vortex preventer</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Fire truck accessories (siameses, standpipes, suction strainers)</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Yes — dedicated category</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">SQD100-1.6 fire pump adapter (siamese); no standpipe/suction strainer lines</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Extinguisher cabinets &amp; portable extinguishers</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Fire cabinets published; portable extinguishers not in published range</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Yes — stainless/metal extinguisher boxes + ABC dry powder extinguishers</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Certifications (published)</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">ISO 9001:2015 (2019); FM/UL products in dedicated category</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">ISO 9001; no FM/UL listings (disclosed)</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">OEM / website</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">OEM/ODM yes; English-only site</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">OEM/ODM yes; 5-language site (EN/ES/RU/FR/AR)</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>

			<h2 id="monitors-deep-dive" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">4. Fire Monitors: The Head-to-Head</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">This is where the two companies meet most directly — and where the difference is a <em>shape of catalog</em>, not a fight over the same SKU. Forede's monitor range is built for breadth: fixed manual and fixed remote monitors (including a wireless remote model at 1200–2400 LPM and stainless-steel 3000/4800 LPM units), portable monitors for wildland use, hydrant-mount monitors with GOST and BS 336 connections, trailer-mounted units, elevated manual monitors, monitor nozzles, water-powered oscillators — and on top of that a separate fire-truck water cannon line (manual, electric, pneumatic, hydraulic) with rotating joints. If your tender lists monitors by flow rate, mounting style or truck integration, Forede's 92-page catalog is the one you will find easier to match line by line.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Wanlian Fluid's monitor line is narrower but deeper in one specific direction: the <a href="/products/auto-tracking-jet-suppression-cannon-zdms/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">ZDMS series auto-tracking jet suppression cannon</a>, where flame detection and self-positioning are the product's core function — the machine finds the fire and tracks it without an operator at the joystick — plus the manual PS series for conventional fixed protection. If your project is a tank farm, jetty, chemical storage area or fuel depot where unattended automatic suppression is the specification, that is the exact product class to shortlist, and it is what we would push you to test against Forede's automatic monitor options side by side.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Fair summary:</strong> breadth of monitor catalog — Forede; flame-tracking automatic cannons as a core line — Wanlian Fluid. For a mixed project, it is legitimate to take truck cannons from one source and the auto-tracking cannon from the other.</p>

			<h2 id="quality-and-certifications" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">5. Quality Systems &amp; Certifications</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>Forede</strong> holds ISO 9001:2015 (obtained 2019 per its published timeline) and operates two Chinese production bases plus stated local bases in some countries. Its dedicated <em>UL / FM Equipment</em> category is the credential signal to take seriously: FM alarm check valves, UL FM water flow detectors and FM-listed sprinkler heads are all published there. "Listed" in a category title is not the same as a verified listing on the exact model you order — request the current FM/UL listing certificate by model number and check it against the certificate holder before you specify.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>Wanlian Fluid</strong> operates under an ISO 9001 quality-management system across its own lines and qualified partner capacity, with 100% per-unit shell pressure and air-leakage testing and export documentation coordinated with shipment. We do not hold FM or UL listings, and we do not claim them — the honest gap versus Forede's UL/FM category, and the reason to route any FM-listed line items through a listed source.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Practical advice:</strong> for both factories, run the same verification kit: ISO 9001 scope, per-model test records matched to your destination standard, listing certificates where claimed, third-party inspection (SGS/BV/TÜV) on a first order, and a sample unit before volume. Our <a href="/guides/how-to-verify-chinese-valve-supplier/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">Chinese supplier verification guide</a> and <a href="/guides/detect-fake-valves-fire-equipment-counterfeits/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">fake-certificate detection guide</a> walk through each check.</p>

			<h2 id="where-each-wins" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">6. Where Each Manufacturer Wins</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>Forede wins when:</strong> the project is fire-truck-centric (truck-mounted cannons in manual/electric/pneumatic/hydraulic, siameses, standpipes, suction strainers, dividers); you need handline and selectable nozzles in depth; the scope is foam end-to-end including AFFF concentrate; you want FM/UL-listed alarm check valves or water flow detectors as published line items (pending per-model verification); or you are matching a tender line-by-line against a very large monitor catalog.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>Wanlian Fluid wins when:</strong> the centerpiece is the <a href="/products/auto-tracking-jet-suppression-cannon-zdms/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">ZDMS auto-tracking cannon</a> (flame detection, self-positioning) for unattended industrial protection; you need <a href="/products/iot-smart-ground-fire-hydrant-ss100zn/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">IoT smart hydrants</a> for a connected municipal network — a line Forede does not publish; you need hydraulic water-level control (F745X) or remote float (100X) valves; your kit includes extinguisher boxes and <a href="/products/abc-dry-powder-fire-extinguisher-5kg/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">ABC portable extinguishers</a>; or you are building a distribution brand in Spanish-, Russian-, French- or Arabic-speaking markets and want localized brand assets and a 5-language technical site.</p>
		<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>They coexist well:</strong> the two companies' overlaps (alarm check valves, gate valves, hydrants, hose reels, manual monitors) are exactly where a competitive quote from both is worthwhile, while their non-overlapping lines (truck accessories + foam concentrate vs. auto-tracking cannons + IoT hydrants + extinguisher kits) can legitimately share one project's bill of materials.</p>

			<h2 id="which-should-you-choose" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">7. Which One Should You Choose?</h2>
			<div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-6 my-5">
				<p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Choose <strong class="text-brand-blue">Forede</strong> when:</p>
				<ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-2">
					<li>Your scope is fire-truck-centric: truck-mounted water cannons, siameses, standpipes, suction strainers, dividers.</li>
					<li>You need foam systems end-to-end, including AFFF foam concentrate from the same supplier.</li>
					<li>Your specification calls for FM/UL-listed alarm check valves or water flow detectors as published line items — then verify the listing per model.</li>
					<li>You want to match a large tender line-by-line against the deepest monitor catalog (92 product pages).</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-6 my-5">
				<p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Choose <strong class="text-brand-red">Wanlian Fluid</strong> when:</p>
				<ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-2">
					<li>The project centers on automatic flame-tracking water cannons (ZDMS) for tank farms, jetties and chemical depots — unattended suppression.</li>
					<li>You need IoT smart hydrants for a connected municipal network, a line Forede does not publish.</li>
					<li>Your BOM includes hydraulic water-level control or remote float valves, extinguisher boxes and ABC extinguishers — a full kit under one PO.</li>
					<li>You are building a distribution brand in ES/RU/FR/AR markets and want localized brand assets plus a 5-language technical site.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">The fastest way to decide: write down (1) whether "fire truck" or "foam concentrate" appears in your scope, (2) whether "auto-tracking" or "flame detection" appears anywhere, and (3) whether your end buyers need documentation in Spanish, Russian, French or Arabic. Point (1) favors Forede; points (2) and (3) favor Wanlian Fluid. Related comparisons: <a href="/guides/wanlian-fluid-vs-ca-fire/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">Wanlian vs CA-FIRE</a> and <a href="/guides/wanlian-fluid-vs-american-avk/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">Wanlian vs American AVK</a>; the general framework is in our <a href="/guides/b2b-valve-sourcing-checklist/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">B2B valve sourcing checklist</a>.</p>

			<!-- FAQ Section -->
			<h2 id="faq" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-6 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
			<div class="space-y-4">
				{faq.map(item => (
					<details class="group bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 p-5 open:border-brand-red/30">
